00:29:14,990 --> 00:29:20,630
and in general Rust strategy that the compiler tries to be as boring.

455
00:29:20,630 --> 00:29:23,111
as possible at the back end. It generates binary code.

456
00:29:23,111 --> 00:29:28,630
It debugs using dwarf, like the dwarf annotations, like the metadata format.

457
00:29:28,630 --> 00:29:32,110
And all of these things, so it's very boring in the back end,

458
00:29:32,110 --> 00:29:34,310
which means most tools can pick up a Rust binary.

